WEBVTT

00:01:43.603 --> 00:01:47.023
Good to see you again,
Ryoma Echizen-<i>kun</i>.

00:01:53.488 --> 00:01:55.573
Who are you?

00:01:56.282 --> 00:02:02.288
"Farewell, Kunimitsu Tezuka"

00:02:10.005 --> 00:02:10.588
"Kunimitsu Tezuka vs. Yudai Yamato"
"S3: Keigo Atobe vs. Kanata Irie"
"D2: ‌Liliadent Krauser vs.
Sotomichi Nakagauchi"

00:02:10.588 --> 00:02:13.800
"S2: Kunimitsu Tezuka vs. Yudai Yamato"
"D1: Senri Chitose vs. Shun Suzuki"
"S1: Keigo Atobe vs. Kanata Irie"

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:15.427
"D2: ‌Liliadent Krauser vs.
Sotomichi Nakagauchi"
"S2: Kunimitsu Tezuka vs. Yudai Yamato"
"D1: Senri Chitose vs. Shun Suzuki"

00:02:24.477 --> 00:02:30.025
You know why I didn't
choose you, don't you?

00:02:31.151 --> 00:02:34.404
There's a much better place
to die waiting for you.

00:02:35.697 --> 00:02:38.742
Fill in the blanks by then.

00:02:47.625 --> 00:02:52.714
Let the team shuffle between
Court 3 and Court 5 begin.

00:02:56.051 --> 00:02:58.845
Are you sure you don't need
to play in this match, Oni?

00:02:59.763 --> 00:03:01.723
You must be quite confident.

00:03:01.723 --> 00:03:05.185
Huh? We're your opponents.

00:03:05.185 --> 00:03:06.436
Where do you think you're looking?

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:08.104
Oh, sorry.

00:03:08.104 --> 00:03:09.981
But, like I said yesterday,

00:03:09.981 --> 00:03:14.611
you don't have nearly enough
skill to play against Court 3.

00:03:15.653 --> 00:03:17.781
You should see what we can do.

00:03:19.157 --> 00:03:20.325
I will.

00:03:24.371 --> 00:03:27.999
It's you, Captain Yamato.

00:03:28.583 --> 00:03:29.542
Well, well.

00:03:29.542 --> 00:03:33.254
I'm surprised you recognized
me without my glasses.

00:03:33.922 --> 00:03:36.174
There is no way I wouldn't recognize the

00:03:36.591 --> 00:03:38.385
former captain of the Seigaku team.

00:03:40.178 --> 00:03:44.307
You haven't changed, Tezuka-<i>kun</i>.

00:03:44.557 --> 00:03:47.811
I look forward to today's match.

00:03:56.653 --> 00:03:57.570
What are these?

00:03:58.154 --> 00:04:00.615
Muscle strengthening rackets.

00:04:00.615 --> 00:04:02.575
Muscle strengthening rackets?

00:04:03.868 --> 00:04:06.830
Everyone grab a racket.

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:12.168
Wh-What's with this thing?

00:04:17.298 --> 00:04:20.010
It's heavy as a rock.

00:04:21.803 --> 00:04:25.181
Those racket frames are filled with lead.

00:04:25.473 --> 00:04:28.059
Takes a lot to just stand while
holding one, doesn't it?

00:04:28.059 --> 00:04:29.102
Hey.

00:04:31.396 --> 00:04:33.648
Let's get on with the training.

00:04:41.656 --> 00:04:42.824
Uza-Uza!

00:04:46.911 --> 00:04:48.329
Because his opponent Liliadent Krauser

00:04:48.329 --> 00:04:50.665
appears unable to continue,

00:04:50.665 --> 00:04:53.752
Court 3's Sotomichi Nakagauchi wins.

00:04:59.299 --> 00:05:02.677
He'll get even stronger.

00:05:03.053 --> 00:05:04.304
Of course.

00:05:08.516 --> 00:05:11.978
The second match is doubles 2.

00:05:16.524 --> 00:05:19.277
Game and match, Shiraishi and Kirihara.

00:05:19.277 --> 00:05:20.820
Six games to four.

00:05:23.198 --> 00:05:26.868
All right! We beat Court 3!

00:05:26.868 --> 00:05:29.079
It's one apiece now.

00:05:29.621 --> 00:05:32.123
Well, how unexpected.

00:05:34.751 --> 00:05:36.836
Is something wrong, Yamato-<i>kun</i>?

00:05:37.212 --> 00:05:38.380
It's your turn.

00:05:40.006 --> 00:05:42.467
When I was a third year middle schooler,

00:05:42.467 --> 00:05:44.302
he was still a first year.

00:05:45.345 --> 00:05:47.263
I have to go give him something he forgot.

00:05:48.682 --> 00:05:50.600
Go ahead, Yamato-<i>kun</i>.

00:05:51.935 --> 00:05:53.520
Hey, Tezuka-<i>san</i>.

00:05:54.437 --> 00:05:57.857
Our next opponent's the former
Seigaku team captain, isn't he?

00:05:57.857 --> 00:05:58.817
Yes.

00:05:58.817 --> 00:06:03.071
I heard you demolished him
when you were a first year.

00:06:03.071 --> 00:06:04.781
This should be an easy win.

00:06:10.537 --> 00:06:11.329
No.

00:06:14.457 --> 00:06:19.462
Tezuka-<i>kun</i>, congratulations on
your national championship.

00:06:19.462 --> 00:06:20.672
Thank you.

00:06:21.214 --> 00:06:24.592
By the way, what are you doing here?

00:06:25.385 --> 00:06:30.056
I heard a professional
German team recruited you.

00:06:30.724 --> 00:06:33.768
I thought you would've
been in Germany by now.

00:06:34.519 --> 00:06:35.770
Germany?

00:06:35.770 --> 00:06:39.774
Tezuka-<i>kun</i>, you were scouted
by a professional team?

00:06:39.774 --> 00:06:41.943
It's a great deal.

00:06:41.943 --> 00:06:44.237
Why don't you join them?

00:06:44.237 --> 00:06:48.116
Doing my best as a U-17 representative

00:06:48.116 --> 00:06:49.993
is the only thing on my mind right now.

00:06:51.411 --> 00:06:52.704
Oh, brother.

00:06:52.704 --> 00:06:54.706
You want to go straight from
being Seigaku's pillar

00:06:54.706 --> 00:06:57.250
to being the Japanese
junior team's pillar?

00:06:57.792 --> 00:06:59.502
Honestly, that is just like you.

00:07:00.420 --> 00:07:01.713
Well, fine.

00:07:02.505 --> 00:07:05.467
As the former and current
captains of the Seigaku team,

00:07:05.467 --> 00:07:07.761
let's enjoy some tennis.

00:07:08.345 --> 00:07:09.220
All right?

00:07:14.100 --> 00:07:15.393
Come on, come on.

00:07:15.393 --> 00:07:18.229
Hurry up and get those balls.

00:07:18.229 --> 00:07:19.272
Let's go.

00:07:23.818 --> 00:07:29.657
Yeah, but with these heavy rackets...

00:07:30.492 --> 00:07:32.702
We can barely move.

00:07:43.338 --> 00:07:47.509
Echizen seems really into it.

00:07:56.685 --> 00:07:58.561
Who are you?

00:07:59.938 --> 00:08:01.231
You don't recognize me?

00:08:01.606 --> 00:08:04.192
How about now?

00:08:06.236 --> 00:08:08.279
Seems you remember me.

00:08:08.863 --> 00:08:11.324
I'm going to play against
Tezuka-<i>kun </i>today.

00:08:11.324 --> 00:08:12.575
Would you like to come watch?

00:08:13.535 --> 00:08:14.744
It's got nothing to do with me.

00:08:15.370 --> 00:08:18.540
Besides, I've got training here.

00:08:19.708 --> 00:08:24.963
It may be Tezuka-<i>kun</i>'s
last match in Japan.

00:08:24.963 --> 00:08:25.922
What?

00:08:37.267 --> 00:08:40.645
Hey, Echizen, don't you think you're
putting a little too much into this?

00:08:40.645 --> 00:08:41.312
I'm fine.

00:08:41.980 --> 00:08:43.231
One more!

00:08:49.279 --> 00:08:51.448
I'm a little nervous.

00:08:51.823 --> 00:08:54.868
It's been a while since we
last played each other.

00:08:57.412 --> 00:08:59.205
Smile.

00:09:01.249 --> 00:09:03.918
I suppose that wouldn't work on you.

00:09:09.966 --> 00:09:11.134
Fifteen-love.

00:09:14.763 --> 00:09:18.850
This is completely different from
the last time we played together.

00:09:22.562 --> 00:09:23.563
Thirty-love.

00:09:25.398 --> 00:09:26.399
Forty-love.

00:09:28.443 --> 00:09:29.569
Game, Tezuka.

00:09:29.569 --> 00:09:30.695
One game to love.

00:09:31.696 --> 00:09:34.783
Hey, Yamato, your junior's beating you.

00:09:34.783 --> 00:09:36.826
Get your shit together.

00:09:37.369 --> 00:09:38.244
Yeah.

00:09:38.745 --> 00:09:40.038
Well, then.

00:09:40.789 --> 00:09:43.708
At this rate, I'll lose
this match in no time.

00:09:49.839 --> 00:09:51.341
I have no choice.

00:09:51.800 --> 00:09:53.885
I'll have to use my special technique.

00:09:55.512 --> 00:09:57.222
Your special technique?

00:10:02.102 --> 00:10:03.353
Here I come.

00:10:11.945 --> 00:10:12.862
What?

00:10:16.533 --> 00:10:17.784
Fifteen-love.

00:10:19.828 --> 00:10:22.414
Tezuka-<i>san</i>... whiffed?

00:10:22.914 --> 00:10:26.251
And he swung when he
was far from the ball.

00:10:27.419 --> 00:10:28.753
What's going on?

00:10:30.547 --> 00:10:34.801
I should've hit that ball.

00:10:35.468 --> 00:10:37.929
Everything you see is an illusion

00:10:37.929 --> 00:10:40.557
produced by direct and indirect factors.

00:10:40.557 --> 00:10:42.809
Is it a dream, or is it reality?

00:10:44.185 --> 00:10:45.520
Let's see...

00:10:47.105 --> 00:10:50.984
Perhaps I should call it
"Illusion to Waking Dream."

00:10:51.234 --> 00:10:53.153
Illusion to Waking Dream?

00:10:53.153 --> 00:10:57.490
What did that Yamato guy do?

00:11:12.297 --> 00:11:15.467
The ball passed through the
strings and disappeared.

00:11:16.676 --> 00:11:17.677
Thirty-love.

00:11:21.389 --> 00:11:22.223
Forty-love.

00:11:32.317 --> 00:11:34.652
Game, Yamato. One game all.

00:11:35.528 --> 00:11:38.365
He caught up in a second.

00:11:38.698 --> 00:11:41.201
I see how it is.

00:11:41.868 --> 00:11:44.788
What? Did you figure something out?

00:11:46.873 --> 00:11:50.377
Tezuka's being manipulated by
a ball that doesn't even exist.

00:11:50.877 --> 00:11:52.629
It doesn't exist?

00:11:54.297 --> 00:11:58.426
Tezuka-<i>kun</i>, you anticipate
where and how your opponent

00:11:58.426 --> 00:12:00.387
will hit the ball by monitoring
their movements and breathing.

00:12:00.762 --> 00:12:05.809
Without realizing it, you predict the
ball's path and move accordingly.

00:12:06.476 --> 00:12:08.186
It's an amazing ability.

00:12:08.728 --> 00:12:11.856
However, sometimes it's
also your weakness.

00:12:12.941 --> 00:12:17.445
That's right. I am using
your ability against you.

00:12:17.445 --> 00:12:20.532
By changing the path of
the ball just as I hit it...

00:12:21.199 --> 00:12:24.369
...you end up chasing a ball
that doesn't even exist.

00:12:31.960 --> 00:12:33.211
Game, Yamato.

00:12:33.211 --> 00:12:34.504
Two games to one.

00:12:35.130 --> 00:12:41.386
I'm amazed Yamato had a trick
like this up his sleeve.

00:12:43.680 --> 00:12:44.639
Tezuka-<i>kun</i>.

00:12:45.640 --> 00:12:47.142
It's an illusion.

00:12:47.600 --> 00:12:49.436
Both the ball you're chasing...

00:12:49.936 --> 00:12:53.523
and the pillar you stand for.

00:13:02.449 --> 00:13:03.533
Tezuka-<i>kun</i>.

00:13:04.367 --> 00:13:06.911
You feel more responsibility
than anyone else.

00:13:07.495 --> 00:13:10.248
You have to be the team's pillar.

00:13:10.665 --> 00:13:12.584
Isn't that what you believe?

00:13:13.376 --> 00:13:18.715
Perhaps it's time you started
fighting for yourself.

00:13:19.090 --> 00:13:21.509
Thank you for the advice.

00:13:22.010 --> 00:13:25.513
However, the hopes of
everyone in Court 5...

00:13:25.930 --> 00:13:29.726
No, all the middle schoolers,
are riding on this match.

00:13:30.143 --> 00:13:31.728
I cannot lose.

00:13:32.854 --> 00:13:33.938
I see.

00:13:34.397 --> 00:13:38.068
You're not willing to let
go of the team's victory.

00:13:46.785 --> 00:13:47.827
That's...

00:13:48.244 --> 00:13:49.621
Tezuka Phantom.

00:13:50.080 --> 00:13:52.207
It's a technique that can

00:13:52.207 --> 00:13:54.918
deflect all his opponent's
balls out of the court.

00:13:59.422 --> 00:14:01.132
Come on, come on!

00:14:14.979 --> 00:14:17.857
All right, 30 minute break.

00:14:19.317 --> 00:14:21.069
Thank goodness.

00:14:21.069 --> 00:14:24.656
That man's no ordinary human.

00:14:24.656 --> 00:14:26.908
He's holding the same racket we are,

00:14:26.908 --> 00:14:29.327
but he's not even breaking a sweat.

00:14:30.370 --> 00:14:32.455
Get out of here. You're an eyesore.

00:14:33.081 --> 00:14:33.748
Huh?

00:14:34.290 --> 00:14:37.877
I can tell you're motivated
by negative thoughts.

00:14:37.877 --> 00:14:40.672
Go flush them out of your system.

00:14:48.888 --> 00:14:52.267
The illusionary balls and the real ones...

00:14:52.976 --> 00:14:55.353
He's deflecting all of them.

00:14:55.353 --> 00:14:56.855
Yeah, but that technique's

00:14:56.855 --> 00:14:59.315
gotta be doing a number on his elbow.

00:15:00.400 --> 00:15:01.401
Tezuka!

00:15:02.027 --> 00:15:03.528
Don't push yourself too hard.

00:15:03.528 --> 00:15:05.655
What'll you do if you
hurt your arm again?

00:15:14.414 --> 00:15:15.498
Out.

00:15:15.498 --> 00:15:16.708
Game, Tezuka.

00:15:16.708 --> 00:15:18.126
Four games to all.

00:15:23.548 --> 00:15:26.634
Tezuka-<i>kun</i>, you...

00:15:29.304 --> 00:15:30.388
Tezuka-<i>kun</i>.

00:15:30.847 --> 00:15:33.099
Do you remember the first time we met?

00:15:34.642 --> 00:15:38.772
I was suffering from a series of injuries.

00:15:41.274 --> 00:15:42.859
Sorry, Yamato.

00:15:43.318 --> 00:15:45.195
We didn't realize you'd been

00:15:45.195 --> 00:15:47.489
hurting your arm so much for Seigaku.

00:15:47.947 --> 00:15:50.450
It's fine. Don't worry about it.

00:15:50.825 --> 00:15:52.827
I chose to do this.

00:15:54.037 --> 00:15:55.997
Despite what I told my teammates,

00:15:56.498 --> 00:16:00.710
the brutal rehabilitation nearly
broke me multiple times.

00:16:02.128 --> 00:16:05.298
Then you appeared.

00:16:07.008 --> 00:16:07.509
"Yamato"

00:16:07.509 --> 00:16:08.760
"Yamato"
Are you sure, Yamato?

00:16:08.760 --> 00:16:11.888
"Yamato"
If your arm wasn't injured,
that first year wouldn't even...

00:16:11.888 --> 00:16:13.765
No, he's strong.

00:16:16.351 --> 00:16:17.352
Tezuka-<i>kun</i>.

00:16:18.311 --> 00:16:21.648
You will become the pillar of Seigaku.

00:16:25.068 --> 00:16:26.778
Thanks to you,

00:16:26.778 --> 00:16:29.406
I regained my passion for tennis,

00:16:30.031 --> 00:16:32.784
and I was able to endure
my painful rehabilitation.

00:16:34.119 --> 00:16:35.328
That's why...

00:16:37.038 --> 00:16:40.834
I don't want you to end up like me.

00:16:45.964 --> 00:16:51.261
You've always sacrificed yourself
for the sake of the team.

00:16:52.137 --> 00:16:54.973
Isn't it time you set yourself free?

00:16:56.683 --> 00:17:00.562
Starting now, fight for only yourself.

00:17:03.565 --> 00:17:04.607
Tezuka!

00:17:05.775 --> 00:17:10.071
You're not the only one
who can be a pillar.

00:17:11.322 --> 00:17:14.284
Have a little faith in us.

00:17:15.785 --> 00:17:16.828
Guys.

00:17:19.247 --> 00:17:22.417
Will you let me enjoy tennis

00:17:23.918 --> 00:17:25.003
a little more?

00:17:26.129 --> 00:17:27.797
Yes. Of course.

00:17:36.598 --> 00:17:39.267
Tezuka-<i>kun</i>, you seem to be having fun.

00:17:39.851 --> 00:17:43.104
Are you ready for my
Illusion to Waking Dream?

00:17:45.148 --> 00:17:46.816
Illusions again?

00:17:47.233 --> 00:17:50.612
No, Tezuka's practically
an illusion himself.

00:17:53.156 --> 00:17:54.449
Game, Tezuka.

00:17:54.449 --> 00:17:56.076
Five games to four.

00:17:59.329 --> 00:18:02.248
It seems I've awakened
a sleeping dragon.

00:18:03.667 --> 00:18:08.505
He completely destroyed Yamato's
Illusion to Waking Dream.

00:18:08.922 --> 00:18:12.425
This is Kunimitsu Tezuka's
true strength.

00:18:12.425 --> 00:18:13.718
Not quite.

00:18:17.597 --> 00:18:21.184
His true strength's
a lot greater than that.

00:18:21.184 --> 00:18:23.436
Tokugawa, what do you think?

00:18:32.362 --> 00:18:35.198
Tezuka, you...

00:18:45.792 --> 00:18:50.296
I'll take the title of pillar
of Seigaku from you.

00:18:53.800 --> 00:18:54.801
That's right.

00:18:55.927 --> 00:18:59.389
My job is done.

00:19:06.438 --> 00:19:08.690
That's the technique Echizen performed

00:19:08.690 --> 00:19:10.108
at the national championship match.

00:19:10.108 --> 00:19:13.820
No, this aura's a lot more powerful.

00:19:13.820 --> 00:19:17.782
The pinnacle of tennis achievable
only by the chosen few.

00:19:20.869 --> 00:19:23.121
The Pinnacle of Perfection.

00:19:50.940 --> 00:19:52.525
Game and match, Tezuka.

00:19:52.525 --> 00:19:54.194
Six games to four.

00:19:58.740 --> 00:20:00.116
Thank you.

00:20:00.617 --> 00:20:03.119
I am grateful for your guidance.

00:20:03.119 --> 00:20:05.789
Not at all. I had fun, too.

00:20:06.164 --> 00:20:07.999
I ended up losing, though.

00:20:09.584 --> 00:20:14.005
Following the path you believe in
isn't a bad thing, you know.

00:20:20.011 --> 00:20:22.013
You did it, Tezuka-<i>kun</i>.

00:20:22.013 --> 00:20:25.433
That guy has no limits.

00:20:26.434 --> 00:20:29.479
I'll catch up to him someday.

00:20:32.774 --> 00:20:34.984
You want to go to Germany, don't you?

00:20:36.236 --> 00:20:39.698
Go and become a professional already.

00:20:41.032 --> 00:20:41.908
Atobe.

00:20:43.702 --> 00:20:45.787
I'll follow you soon enough.

00:20:53.712 --> 00:20:55.505
You came to watch the match.

00:20:58.383 --> 00:21:01.761
I'm glad I followed the path I believed in.

00:21:02.429 --> 00:21:04.514
Today confirmed it.

00:21:05.682 --> 00:21:08.768
I want you to follow the
path you believe in as well.

00:21:11.062 --> 00:21:12.313
It was a great match.

00:21:14.232 --> 00:21:15.483
Thank you.

00:21:16.860 --> 00:21:20.113
It was a good retirement match.

00:21:28.913 --> 00:21:30.123
Hey.

00:23:17.063 --> 00:23:19.649
"Preview"

00:23:19.649 --> 00:23:20.567
"Preview"
I can't believe I'm losing
to a middle schooler.

00:23:20.567 --> 00:23:22.652
I can't believe I'm losing
to a middle schooler.

00:23:22.652 --> 00:23:26.364
This game's already over
if you're worried about that.

00:23:26.698 --> 00:23:29.659
My growth accelerates by the day.

00:23:29.659 --> 00:23:32.662
Damn it. Does it all end here?

00:23:34.039 --> 00:23:35.248
You're finished.

00:23:35.248 --> 00:23:37.625
I'll use my insight to
perceive your blind spots...

00:23:38.084 --> 00:23:39.627
You have none!

00:23:42.172 --> 00:23:43.423
"Promise"
The next episode of
<i>Prince of Tennis II </i>is: "Promise."

00:23:43.423 --> 00:23:47.136
"Promise"
Oh, you noticed?
